# 37. Important Development Rules
Follow these rules throughout development:
1. Use TypeScript.
2. Write production-quality code.
3. Follow SOLID principles where appropriate.
4. Keep components small and reusable.
5. Do not duplicate code.
6. Do not put business logic inside React components.
7. Do not put business logic directly inside Express controllers.
8. Validate all API inputs.
9. Use proper HTTP status codes.
10. Handle errors centrally.
11. Use MongoDB indexes appropriately.
12. Use pagination for large datasets.
13. Do not expose secrets.
14. Keep environment-specific configuration in `.env`.
15. Make the application responsive.
16. Make accessibility a consideration.
17. Use meaningful variable and function names.
18. Add comments only where they provide real value.
19. Prefer maintainability over clever code.
20. Do not over-engineer simple features.

