The final product should feel like a professional personal ATS + Interview Knowledge Base + Company Targeting + Interview Preparation platform, specifically designed for a software developer's job search.

#One important suggestion
For your use case, I would not make this only an "interview tracker." Make it a combination of:
Personal ATS + Interview Question Bank + Company Targeting + Preparation Tracker + Analytics
The most valuable workflow would be:
Company → Job → Application → Interview → Questions → Performance → Weak Areas → Preparation → Next Target
That creates a feedback loop instead of just storing information.
For example:
> You interview at Company A → save 15 questions → system identifies that you struggled with MongoDB aggregation → MongoDB becomes a weak topic → preparation progress increases → when another company requires MongoDB, your skill-match score automatically improves.
That would make your portal genuinely useful rather than just another CRUD project.
